<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Roxas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1892–1948</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Roxas was the first president of the independent Republic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, taking office in 1946 after serving as the last president of the Commonwealth. He led reconstruction after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and signed agreements giving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> trade privileges and military bases. He died in office in 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-roxas.jpg" alt="Manuel Roxas" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hessler Studio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manuel_Roxas_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
